[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Document and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and
[stderr] resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization
[stderr] role, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local
[stderr] campaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain
[stderr] GATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,
[stderr] privacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `docs/security-boundary.md`.
[stderr] - `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.
[stderr] - The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity
[stderr]   contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] State that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account
[stderr] or authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has
[stderr] no remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud
[stderr] backup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque
[stderr] local reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote
[stderr] profile fields.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Add negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation
[stderr] modules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or
[stderr] server clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,
[stderr] purchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if
[stderr] ever approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] Responsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same
[stderr] connected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage
[stderr] do not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target
