[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Specify the bounded, local save and recovery protocol for immutable revisions,
[stderr] +checksums, validated current pointers, known-good retention, quarantine,
[stderr] +separate preferences, explicit deletion, and save-safe boundaries. This is a
[stderr] +protocol and fixture contract, not approval to select a browser-storage API or
[stderr] +promise a quota, retention period, or migration-support window.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +R0002 provides the core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic clock and
[stderr] +persistence fixtures, and R0004 supplies the immutable versioned campaign
[stderr] +snapshot and command/revision contracts. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: storage
[stderr] +API, quota, support window, and recovery policy require human approval before
[stderr] +implementation selects or relies on them. The gate blocks implementation
[stderr] +choices, not this contract's authoring.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/` protocol contracts.
[stderr] +- `src/platform/web/persistence/` adapter boundary.
[stderr] +- `tests/{core,platform}/save*` fault and recovery fixtures.
[stderr] +- `docs/save-and-recovery.md`.
[stderr] +- Snapshot/preference/quarantine schemas and snapshot-repository/recovery API.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The shared layer owns snapshot shape, validation, compatibility, and recovery
[stderr] +semantics. The web adapter owns only the eventual approved local-storage
[stderr] +mechanism. PWA cache/install lifecycle, content registry, remote sync,
[stderr] +identity, diagnostics transport, and campaign transitions are not owned here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Use a write-ahead replacement protocol: serialize a complete immutable
[stderr] +snapshot, validate checksum/schema/invariants, write a new revision candidate,
[stderr] +verify read-back, atomically mark a validated current pointer (or emulate it
[stderr] +with immutable records), and retain the prior known-good snapshot. Never clear
[stderr] +or overwrite the prior confirmed save until the new pointer is valid. Separate
[stderr] +preferences from campaign snapshots and never treat a cache record as a save.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Validate bounded, untrusted persisted bytes before parsing or use. A malformed,
[stderr] +checksum-invalid, incompatible, or migration-failed candidate is preserved with
[stderr] +its metadata in quarantine; it never replaces a valid save. Recovery offers
[stderr] +the last valid checkpoint or a clear new-game/fallback route. Loading restores
[stderr] +only safe scene boundaries. A failed quota, permission, or unavailable-storage
[stderr] +attempt leaves the session playable, says persistence did not succeed, and
[stderr] +offers non-blocking retry guidance.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Persist only at explicit safe boundaries: no unresolved combat turn or partial
[stderr] +command can become current. A stale writer must fail rather than replace the
[stderr] +latest revision. Deletion requires an explicit confirmation naming the selected
[stderr] +slot and its available progress/time; initial focus is Cancel, repeated/stale
[stderr] +input cannot activate Delete, and only that local slot and its recovery
[stderr] +metadata are removed.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Migration transformations remain ordered pure candidate transformations and
[stderr] +are not implemented or approved here beyond their compatibility boundary; R0007
[stderr] +owns the migration runner. No cloud, account, sync, cross-device merge, cache
[stderr] +eviction, or export/import promise is introduced.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Web and installed PWA share the same local snapshot, preference, validation,
[stderr] +quarantine, and recovery contract. The web adapter eventually binds an approved
[stderr] +same-origin storage mechanism; the PWA inherits it and must keep its
[stderr] +service-worker cache separate. A cache refresh or update failure neither
[stderr] +deletes, refreshes, nor synchronises save data, and no implementation may
[stderr] +claim persistence after an unconfirmed write.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not choose a storage API, quota, eviction guarantee, support window,
[stderr] +retention policy, or migration set before GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 approval. Do not
[stderr] +implement cloud sync, accounts, remote deletion, cross-device conflict
[stderr] +resolution, PWA cache lifecycle, release update flow, diagnostics transport,
[stderr] +content validation, gameplay, UI screens, product assets, or audio.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: local snapshots, protocol interfaces, and
[stderr] +fault fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental
[stderr] +visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other
[stderr] +product asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Run deterministic fault fixtures for interrupted write, failed read-back,
[stderr] +  checksum failure, malformed/oversized bytes, unsupported version, storage
[stderr] +  quota/permission/unavailable failures, stale writer, quarantine, retry, and
[stderr] +  selected-slot deletion confirmation.
[stderr] +- Prove each failure preserves the last valid snapshot, does not report a save
[stderr] +  as successful, keeps the session usable where possible, and exposes the
[stderr] +  required retry/title/fallback/new-game recovery choice.
[stderr] +- Prove a current-pointer promotion occurs only after candidate validation and
[stderr] +  read-back; prove preferences and PWA cache fixtures cannot be read as or
[stderr] +  overwrite a campaign snapshot.
[stderr] +- Prove a pending command or unresolved combat turn cannot be committed and a
[stderr] +  stale/repeated delete action cannot remove an unselected slot.
[stderr] +- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses
[stderr] +  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0006, dependencies
[stderr] +  match the manifest, owned paths do not overlap R0005's content boundary, and
[stderr] +  every required section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an
[stderr] +  R contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Retain deterministic fault-fixture output, pre/post candidate and pointer
[stderr] +records, quarantine and recovery-path assertions, preference/save/cache
[stderr] +separation evidence, deletion-confirmation assertions, the retained
[stderr] +GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 record, and the pre-checkpoint loader, provenance,
[stderr] +dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Interrupted, invalid, incompatible, or failed save candidates cannot replace
[stderr] +  a validated current snapshot; the prior known-good snapshot is retained or
[stderr] +  malformed bytes are quarantined.
[stderr] +- Save snapshots, preferences, and PWA cache records remain separate, and
[stderr] +  local recovery presents clear retry, title, fallback, or new-game choices
[stderr] +  without claiming an unconfirmed save succeeded.
[stderr] +- Storage selection, quota, support window, migration policy, and recovery
[stderr] +  policy remain blocked by GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no remote, cache, or asset
[stderr] +  work is introduced.
