raction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"valid minimal package passes\",\"invalid references fail\",\"reachability fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0006\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0006\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; protocol is data/recovery only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"fault fixtures cover write and validation failures\",\"save/cache separation\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID; wait for storage decision before accepting gated work\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0007\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0007\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"predecessors migrate once\",\"failed candidate remains intact\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and resume after R0006/gate closure\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0008\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0008\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; a negative scope boundary.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no identity/token/network fields\",\"future connected work remains gated\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0009\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n  ]\n}\n---\ntask_id: R0004\nsequence: 4\ntitle: Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\ndependencies: R0002,R0003\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0001,REQ-0003,REQ-0004,REQ-0006,NFR-0002,NFR-0010\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract,specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0004\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the immutable, versioned shared campaign-state, command, result, event,\nrevision, interaction-ID, and deterministic-RNG contracts needed to validate\nlegal transitions. This foundation defines envelopes and invariants only; it\ndoes not introduce a feature state machine or authored campaign values.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 provides the shared-core/adapter seam and R0003 provides deterministic\nfixtures. They are implementation dependencies, not authoring blockers.\nRetain GATE-0004: concrete party and content shapes remain unapproved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/`.\n- The versioned campaign-snapshot envelope and deterministic RNG state.\n- The public core command, state, event, result, revision, and interaction-ID\n  interfaces, plus `tests/core/contract.*`.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nMake state transitions pure and explicit: a command carries an expected\ncampaign revision and stable interaction/action ID; processing returns either\na typed rejection with no mutation or ordered state/events with a new revision.\nValidate command shape, session state, identifiers, availability, eligibility,\npredicates, and expected revision before any transition. Invariant helpers\nmust reject invalid state and preserve the prior immutable state.\n\nRecord deterministic RNG seed/state at safe boundaries. Require idempotency for\nretries: a duplicate interaction ID or acknowledged durable transition returns\nits prior result without a second reward, checkpoint, or revision-changing\ntransition. Process one command at a time per active campaign and reject stale\nwriters so visibility changes, repeated input, and concurrent tabs cannot\ninterleave a transition.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nWeb and PWA adapters submit the same shared command envelopes and consume the\nsame state/event results. Platform adapters may debounce controls and manage a\nlocal slot lease/read-only warning, but neither gains authority to mutate state\ndirectly. Installation, cache lifecycle, and storage-driver work are outside\nthis contract.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not author content values; implement combat, inventory, quest, exploration,\nor UI state machines; select party shapes; implement a save driver or cache;\nadd account, identity, token, role, network, or remote state; or create assets,\naudio, maps, dialogue, or reference-derived content.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: these serializable state and interface\ncontracts deliberately exclude authored content. Do not create or reserve\nincidental visual, source, audio, font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite,\nmap, or other product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Use R0003 deterministic fixtures to prove invalid commands leave the exact\n  prior state unchanged and stale revisions reject without mutation.\n- Prove a duplicate interaction ID returns the recorded prior outcome and\n  produces no additional durable transition.\n- Exercise controlled RNG state twice and compare state/event results.\n- Exercise sequential command handling and a stale-writer fixture without\n  selecting a browser-storage implementation.\n- Record GATE-0004 as retained before adding concrete party/content shapes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain contract-test output for invalid, stale, duplicate, deterministic-RNG,\nand serialized transition cases, plus the public envelope/invariant inventory\nand the retained GATE-0004 record.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Invalid or stale commands cannot mutate campaign state.\n- Duplicate interaction IDs are idempotent and cause no extra durable\n  transition.\n- State, command, result, event, revision, and RNG contracts are shared-core\n  only, versioned where serialized, and independent of concrete content,\n  persistence drivers, or connected scope.\nsed: projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/README.md: No such file or directory\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 3 'versioned-content-and-save-schemas|persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics|save-recovery-and-offline-persistence|empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/TEMPLATE.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/F014.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md && rg -n -C 2 'IMP-0005|IMP-0006|GATE-0003' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n exited 1 in 0ms:\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4 | rg '(\"'^|/)(TEMPLATE|F014|implementation-catalogue-index|02-feature-model|03-technical-contract|04-experience-contract|R0008)'\"\\\\.md\"'$|implementation-catalogue-index'\"\\\\.json\"'$'\"'\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -C 3 'versioned content|save schemas|persistence, migration|save recovery|empty, error|GATE-0003' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/{02-feature-model,03-technical-contract,04-experience-contract}.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md && sed -n '1,260p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json && sed -n '1,260p' runbooks/TEMPLATE.md && sed -n '1,260p' runbooks/F014.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-19-| Game shell and responsive renderer | J1, J3, J6; readable mobile-to-desktop play | Owns navigation, focus/visibility pause, semantic UI, visual settings, and rendering only. It requests domain commands and renders returned state/events. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-20-| Input adapters | Keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad accessibility | Convert platform events into a shared, remappable `InputAction` vocabulary; unavailable hardware is non-fatal. No adapter may mutate campaign state directly. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-21-| Deterministic rules core | Tutorial combat, quests, inventory, progression | Owns legal state transitions, seeded/randomness policy, combat resolution, reward ledger, and invariants. Command validation precedes every mutation. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:22:| Content registry and validator | One town/dungeon, original content, localisation | Loads the active versioned content package; resolves IDs/keys and rejects invalid packages before play. It is read-only at runtime. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-23-| Save/recovery repository | J5, long-session recovery | Owns atomic local snapshot writes, validation, quarantine, migration, retention, export/import when approved, and explicit deletion. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-24-| PWA release manager | J7, install/offline/update safety | Owns precache manifest, cache integrity, install affordance, and safe-boundary activation. It never replaces a running release or a pending save write. |\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-25-| Error boundary and consent-gated diagnostics | Crash/error recovery and privacy | Shows retry/title/recovery actions. Local diagnostic records are minimal and removable; no telemetry transport exists in P0. |\n--\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-57-until approval defines identity, vendor, consent, cost, retention, deletion,\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-58-support, conflict UX, and outage behaviour.\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-59-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md:60:### Versioned content and save schemas\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-61-\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-62-All high-volume authored data uses a versioned, machine-validated package:\nprojects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md-63-\n---\ntask_id: R0008\nsequence: 8\ntitle: Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\ndependencies: R0002,R0004\nrequirement_ids: REQ-0013,REQ-0014,REQ-0015,NFR-0012\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-0008\nauthoring_batch: B0003\nfactory_stages: F011,F012,F013\nasset_impact: not_applicable\nasset_ids:\nasset_brief: No assets; a negative scope boundary.\naudio_impact: not_applicable\naudio_ids:\naudio_brief:\naudio_duration_seconds: 0\naudio_loop: not_applicable\naudio_style_version:\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDocument and test the P0 negative boundary: local campaign start, save, and\nresume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, authorization\nrole, entitlement, multiplayer, moderation, safety, or connected service.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nR0002 supplies the core/adapter dependency seam and R0004 supplies the local\ncampaign state envelope. They are implementation dependencies. Retain\nGATE-0006 / DEC-0006: no connected feature may be implemented until its scope,\nprivacy, security, operational, cost, and failure-mode decisions are approved.\n\n## Ownership\n\n- `docs/security-boundary.md`.\n- `tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*`.\n- The future connected-service approval checklist and local-slot identity\n  contract.\n\n## Required behaviour\n\nState that the local browser profile is the P0 player boundary, not an account\nor authorization guarantee. The local campaign is the source of truth and has\nno remote profile, analytics stream, purchase ledger, match state, cloud\nbackup, role, privilege, or entitlement. Local slot selection is an opaque\nlocal reference only and must not contain identity, token, privilege, or remote\nprofile fields.\n\nAdd negative contract tests and a static boundary scan for P0 foundation\nmodules. They must fail on identity/token/role/entitlement fields, network or\nserver clients, sign-in/OAuth/sync paths, multiplayer/safety/moderation APIs,\npurchase flows, or remote campaign authority. Treat future replication, if\never approved, as a separate optional mirror rather than campaign truth.\n\n## Web and PWA differences\n\nResponsive web and installed PWA use the same local-slot contract and same\nconnected-scope exclusion. PWA installation, cache, and browser-origin storage\ndo not imply identity, authorization, sync, or a remote service. No target\nobtains a distinct connected implementation path.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not implement sign-in, OAuth, accounts, profiles, tokens, roles,\nauthorization, synchronization, server APIs, analytics transport, multiplayer,\nmoderation, reporting, purchases, entitlements, cloud saves, remote\ndiagnostics, or security claims about a device owner. Do not create product\nassets, audio, or connected-service configuration.\n\n## Asset assessment\n\n`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this is documentation and negative test\ncoverage for an architectural exclusion. Do not create or reserve incidental\nvisual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or\nother product assets; `asset_ids` remains blank.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Run a static scan across P0 foundation modules for prohibited identity,\n  token, privilege, entitlement, and network/server-client fields or imports.\n- Run negative fixtures that attempt prohibited connected-scope configuration\n  and prove the contract rejects or does not expose it.\n- Verify start, local save, and local resume fixtures require only a local slot\n  reference and no remote request or account data.\n- Review `docs/security-boundary.md` against the exclusion list and record\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 as retained for any future connected proposal.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRetain static-scan and negative-fixture results, local start/save/resume test\noutput showing no remote request, the security-boundary review, and the future\nconnected-service approval checklist with its retained gate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- P0 start, save, and resume expose no identity, token, role, entitlement,\n  remote-profile, or network-client field or dependency.\n- Negative tests prevent connected-service scope from entering P0 foundation\n  modules for both web and PWA delivery paths.\n- Any future connected work remains outside campaign truth and blocked by\n  GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 rather than implicitly approved.\n{\n  \"catalogue_id\": \"mock-fantasy-quest-4-implementation-catalogue\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"source\": [\"../specification/README.md\", \"../specification/requirements.json\", \"05-delivery-map.md\", \"06-foundation-domain-contracts.md\", \"07-feature-experience-contracts.md\", \"08-quality-operations-contracts.md\"],\n  \"scope\": \"P0 is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG delivered through a shared web core and a PWA delivery adaptation. Connected services are not P0 implementation scope.\",\n  \"first_bounded_domain\": {\"id\": \"SHARD-01\", \"title\": \"Foundation and core contracts\", \"contract_limit\": 250, \"contract_count\": 12, \"state\": \"ready_for_authoring\", \"boundary\": \"Framework-neutral seams, deterministic state/data contracts, local persistence protocol, quality foundations, and original-design controls; excludes campaign rules, UI flows, PWA lifecycle, and release execution.\"},\n  \"contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A framework-neutral project skeleton documents one bootstrap, lint, format, and deterministic test command with isolated shared, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, content, and test directories.\",\"prerequisites\":[],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"root build/tooling configuration\",\"src/{core,content,app,platform/web,platform/pwa}/\",\"tests/\",\"docs/development.md\"],\"data\":[\"pinned toolchain declaration\"],\"api\":[\"build/test command interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"selecting framework/package manager/CI without DEC-0001\",\"gameplay\",\"service worker\",\"hosting\"],\"verification\":\"Clean approved-runtime checkout runs the documented deterministic sample test, lint, and format checks.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 framework, package-manager, and CI selection before implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"domain\":\"foundation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"REQ-0013\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A dependency policy and public interfaces prevent core code from importing browser, renderer, clock, network, or platform modules; adapters submit commands and render returned state/events.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/public interfaces\",\"src/platform/{web,pwa}/adapter interfaces\",\"architecture dependency rules\",\"docs/architecture.md\"],\"data\":[\"dependency-policy manifest\"],\"api\":[\"Command, state, event, and adapter interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"concrete combat/exploration/UI\",\"account or network client\",\"target-specific campaign rules\"],\"verification\":\"A dependency-rule test rejects forbidden core imports and a fixture adapter proves command-only interaction.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; retain GATE-0001 for tool-specific enforcement.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"domain\":\"tests\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test conventions provide isolated RNG/clock and persistence fixtures with no real service or player data access.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"test-runner configuration\",\"tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures\",\"docs/testing.md\"],\"data\":[\"deterministic fixture factories\"],\"api\":[\"test fixture and fake clock/RNG interfaces\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"final feature assertions\",\"real browser/device matrix claims\",\"production telemetry\"],\"verification\":\"Repeated core fixture execution has identical results; a deliberately failing fixture is detected; fixture storage is isolated.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 before compatibility or performance claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"domain\":\"data\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0010\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Immutable versioned state, command/result/event envelopes, revision and interaction identifiers, deterministic RNG state, and invariant helpers define legal transition mechanics without feature state machines.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}/\",\"tests/core/contract.*\"],\"data\":[\"campaign snapshot envelope\",\"deterministic RNG state\"],\"api\":[\"Core command/state/event API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"authored values\",\"combat/inventory/quest algorithms\",\"save driver\",\"UI selection state\",\"account/network state\"],\"verification\":\"Invalid and stale commands do not mutate state; duplicate interaction IDs cause no extra durable transition.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 before concrete party/content shapes.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Typed content-package schema and validator cover IDs, references, locale keys, assets, predicates, rewards, and reachability but contain no authored campaign expression.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/\",\"tests/content/validation.*\",\"docs/content-authoring.md\"],\"data\":[\"versioned content package format\",\"asset/provenance manifest schema\"],\"api\":[\"content registry and validator API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"town/dungeon dialogue/maps/assets\",\"copied reference expression\",\"release packaging\"],\"verification\":\"Valid minimum package passes; each invalid reference class fails; a graph fixture checks opening-to-ending reachability.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0004 for quantities, locale, and content detail; human provenance review remains required.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A schema protocol specifies immutable revisions, checksums, current-pointer validation, known-good retention, quarantine, separate preferences, deletion confirmation, and safe-boundary persistence rules.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0003\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/\",\"src/platform/web/persistence/\",\"tests/{core,platform}/save*\",\"docs/save-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"save snapshot and preference schemas\",\"quarantine record\"],\"api\":[\"snapshot repository and recovery protocol\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"cloud sync\",\"identity\",\"PWA cache records\",\"eviction guarantee\"],\"verification\":\"Fault fixtures cover interrupted write, checksum failure, malformed data, quota/permission failure, quarantine, retry, and selected-slot deletion.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage API, quota, support window, and recovery policy.\",\"complexity\":\"high\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"domain\":\"persistence\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0006\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Ordered, pure migrations declare supported versions and promote only validated candidates while preserving original invalid bytes for quarantine.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/core/save/{migrations,compatibility}/\",\"tests/core/save/fixtures\"],\"data\":[\"migration registry and predecessor fixtures\"],\"api\":[\"migration runner API\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"storage driver changes\",\"future data export\",\"automatic destructive repair\"],\"verification\":\"Every declared predecessor migrates once; unsupported or failed migration leaves the original candidate intact and quarantined.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 support-window approval.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"domain\":\"security\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0013\",\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Architecture and negative contract tests demonstrate that local campaign start/save/resume require no account identifier, token, remote profile, role, entitlement, multiplayer, or safety service.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/security-boundary.md\",\"tests/core/connected-scope-exclusion.*\"],\"data\":[\"future connected-service approval checklist\"],\"api\":[\"local-slot identity contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"sign-in\",\"OAuth\",\"sync\",\"roles\",\"moderation\",\"purchases\",\"server APIs\"],\"verification\":\"Static scan and negative fixtures find no identity/token/privilege fields or network client in P0 foundation modules.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0006 / DEC-0006 before any connected implementation.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"domain\":\"privacy\",\"targets\":[\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0006\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A bounded local diagnostic schema, consent and clear controls, redaction rules, and no-network guardrails support future player recovery without collecting save or dialogue payloads.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0006\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/platform/web/diagnostics/\",\"src/app/recovery/diagnostic-contract.*\",\"tests/platform/diagnostics.*\",\"docs/privacy-and-recovery.md\"],\"data\":[\"redacted local diagnostic record\",\"consent state\"],\"api\":[\"diagnostic recorder interface\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"diagnostic provider/transport\",\"remote analytics\",\"retention promise\",\"secrets\"],\"verification\":\"Tests prove diagnostics are absent without consent, redact payloads, and can be deleted locally.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0005 / DEC-0005 before transport, retention, hosting, or support claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"domain\":\"accessibility\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0010\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Original semantic tokens cover typography, spacing, focus, motion, touch targets, status, contrast, and non-colour cues, enabling later responsive web UI and inherited PWA UI.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"src/app/design/tokens/\",\"docs/design-tokens.md\",\"tests/app/design-tokens.*\"],\"data\":[\"semantic token inventory\"],\"api\":[\"token consumption contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"screens\",\"maps\",\"final artwork/fonts\",\"final breakpoints\",\"copied reference styling\"],\"verification\":\"Token validation proves semantic labels/non-colour cues and reduced-motion values in representative fixtures.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"GATE-0002 and GATE-0004 before numeric contrast/font/breakpoint claims.\",\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"gated\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"domain\":\"content\",\"targets\":[\"shared\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"A provenance record format, review checklist, and source-asset manifest make authorship and permitted functional reference scope auditable before authored content enters a build.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"assets/source-manifest.*\",\"docs/original-content-review.md\",\"tests/content/provenance.*\"],\"data\":[\"provenance manifest and review disposition\"],\"api\":[\"provenance validator input contract\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"creating art/audio/story\",\"licensing approval\",\"automatic legal clearance\"],\"verification\":\"Validator rejects missing provenance fields; human creative review is recorded for each authored package.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"Human creative/provenance review; legal or licensing review if applicable under GATE-0007.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"},\n    {\"id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"domain\":\"documentation\",\"targets\":[\"shared\",\"web\",\"pwa\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"NFR-0012\",\"NFR-0010\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\"],\"bounded_outcome\":\"Developer documentation records ownership, command flow, save-versus-cache separation, deferred connected scope, and the decisions/gates that later domain authors must preserve.\",\"prerequisites\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0008\"],\"ownership\":{\"files\":[\"docs/{architecture,development,save-and-recovery,security-boundary}.md\"],\"data\":[\"foundation decision and ownership index\"],\"api\":[\"documented public-boundary inventory\"]},\"forbidden_scope\":[\"player release guide\",\"operational rollout\",\"claiming approved vendor or policy choices\"],\"verification\":\"Documentation review cross-checks every foundation contract's ownership, dependency, and gate against this catalogue.\",\"human_external_gate\":\"None; approval gates are documented, not resolved.\",\"complexity\":\"low\",\"status\":\"current\"}\n  ],\n  \"expansion_queue\": [\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-02\",\"title\":\"Campaign content and domain logic\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"exploration\",\"dialogue\",\"quests\",\"tutorial\",\"combat\",\"inventory\",\"party progression\",\"town/dungeon/ending content\",\"content validation\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0001\",\"REQ-0002\",\"REQ-0003\",\"REQ-0004\",\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0008\",\"NFR-0007\",\"NFR-0008\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared core and content only; no UI ownership\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-03\",\"title\":\"Session, UI, input, and accessibility\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\"],\"covers\":[\"session/checkpoints\",\"semantic responsive shell\",\"game panels\",\"keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad adapters\",\"settings\",\"localisation\",\"captions\",\"feedback\",\"error recovery UI\",\"accessibility tests\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0005\",\"REQ-0006\",\"REQ-0007\",\"REQ-0009\",\"REQ-0010\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0002\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0004\",\"NFR-0005\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0003,GATE-0004\",\"target_allocation\":\"shared UI model; web input/layout adapter; PWA inherits UI with no separate UI fork\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-04\",\"title\":\"PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\",\"SHARD-02\",\"SHARD-03\"],\"covers\":[\"PWA manifest/install\",\"service-worker cache lifecycle\",\"offline/update recovery\",\"performance measurement\",\"security headers\",\"release checks\",\"observability\",\"quality automation\",\"player/operator documentation\",\"platform certification assessment\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0011\",\"REQ-0012\",\"NFR-0001\",\"NFR-0003\",\"NFR-0006\",\"NFR-0009\",\"NFR-0011\",\"NFR-0012\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0002,GATE-0005,GATE-0007\",\"target_allocation\":\"web release build and PWA service-worker/install adapter are distinct; shared core owns neither cache nor hosting\",\"state\":\"queued\"},\n    {\"id\":\"SHARD-05\",\"title\":\"Connected-scope decision package\",\"max_contracts\":250,\"depends_on\":[\"SHARD-01\"],\"covers\":[\"identity/sync conflict policy\",\"multiplayer/player safety\",\"live operations\",\"commerce/entitlements\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"REQ-0014\",\"REQ-0015\"],\"gate\":\"GATE-0006\",\"target_allocation\":\"no P0 target implementation; research/decision outputs only if explicitly authorised\",\"state\":\"hold\"}\n  ],\n  \"requirement_coverage\": {\n    \"REQ-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-02; provenance foundation IMP-0011\",\"REQ-0002\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0003\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0004\":\"queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0005\":\"queued: SHARD-02 and SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0007\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"REQ-0009\":\"queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0010\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"REQ-0011\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"REQ-0013\":\"current: IMP-0002, IMP-0008\",\"REQ-0014\":\"gated: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"REQ-0015\":\"hold: SHARD-05 / GATE-0006; no P0 implementation\",\"NFR-0001\":\"queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0002\":\"current/gated: IMP-0004, IMP-0006, IMP-0007\",\"NFR-0003\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006, IMP-0007; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0004\":\"current/gated: IMP-0010; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0005\":\"current/gated: IMP-0006; queued: SHARD-03\",\"NFR-0006\":\"current/gated: IMP-0009; queued: SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0007\":\"current: IMP-0005; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0008\":\"current: IMP-0005, IMP-0010, IMP-0011; queued: SHARD-02\",\"NFR-0009\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0002\",\"NFR-0010\":\"current: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0004; queued target adapters in SHARD-03 and SHARD-04\",\"NFR-0011\":\"gated: SHARD-04 / GATE-0005\",\"NFR-0012\":\"current/gated: IMP-0001, IMP-0002, IMP-0003, IMP-0008, IMP-0012; queued: SHARD-04\"\n  },\n  \"dependency_graph\": {\"nodes\":[\"IMP-0001\",\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\",\"IMP-0007\",\"IMP-0008\",\"IMP-0009\",\"IMP-0010\",\"IMP-0011\",\"IMP-0012\"],\"acyclic\":true,\"validation\":\"Each prerequisite points only to an earlier numbered contract; SHARD dependencies only point from later shards to earlier shards.\"}\n}\n---\ntask_id: T001\nsequence: 1\ntitle: Describe one small, reviewable change\nbrowser_impact: none\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nDescribe the smallest complete outcome. State what is in scope and, equally\nimportant, what must not be changed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The intended behaviour is implemented and documented where it affects users or developers.\n- Focused automated tests cover the change and pass.\n- No unrelated refactors, network calls, or credentials are introduced.\n---\ntask_id: F014\nsequence: 14\ntitle: Generate the bounded implementation-runbook authoring collection\nbrowser_impact: not_applicable\nplaywright_spec:\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nGenerate only the bootstrap wave of ordinary Supervisor runbooks in\n`projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks/`: a bounded catalogue-expansion\ntask followed by a dispatcher task. The dispatcher allocates at most ten\nauthoring B-series tasks per wave, creates one successor dispatcher, and stops.\nEach authoring task instructs Codex to create only its assigned R-series\nimplementation runbooks under\n`projects/<project-slug>/runbooks/`, then validate their metadata and update the\nmanifest. The successor dispatcher repeats this process until no queued\ncatalogue chapter or unassigned implementation contract remains. Generate an\n`INITIAL.md` context document in `authoring-runbooks/`\nthat points to the canonical `PROJECT_BRIEF.md` and specification.\n\nRegister the generated authoring collection with the source collection by\nwriting `runbooks/.supervisor-children/<project-slug>.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../projects/<project-slug>/authoring-runbooks\"}`. Also\nwrite `authoring-runbooks/.supervisor-children/implementation.json` containing\n`{\"runbooks_dir\": \"../runbooks\"}`. These are explicit child-collection\nregistrations; `supervisor-run --run-all` follows them automatically after the\nparent collection is accepted.\n\nEvery dispatcher first expands at most one queued specification/catalogue domain\nchapter (maximum 250 `IMP-*` contracts), validates its coverage, then allocates\nready contracts. If any queued chapter or ready contract remains, it creates no\nmore than ten authoring tasks and exactly one successor dispatcher. If none\nremains, it creates the final audit task instead. This is a durable loop, not a\nrecursive prompt or an unbounded single run.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must use the standard Supervisor front matter\nand contain: precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs; owned\nfiles/data/interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; platform differences;\nverification commands/evidence; and observable acceptance criteria. It must be\nsmall enough for one implementation task, not a vague epic.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must retain machine-readable provenance to the\ncanonical decisions that justify it. Its front matter must declare all of these\nnon-empty fields, using comma-separated values where more than one applies:\n\n```yaml\nsource_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#save-state\nsource_catalogue_ids: IMP-SAVE-001\nauthoring_batch: B0007\nfactory_stages: F003,F005,F012,F013\n```\n\n`source_specifications` points to the smallest relevant canonical\nspecification section; `source_catalogue_ids` identifies the allocated\nimplementation-catalogue records; `authoring_batch` identifies the B-series\nwriter that created the R file; and `factory_stages` identifies the F-series\nstages that established the requirement. This is a traceability trail, not an\ninstruction to inject every F or B runbook into the implementation agent's\nprompt. The R task uses these links to read only the canonical context it needs.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also include a detailed asset assessment.\nIts front matter must always declare both fields below, even when no assets are\nneeded:\n\n```yaml\nasset_impact: required # or not_applicable\nasset_ids: village_gate_main,village_gate_construction # blank only when not_applicable\n```\n\nFor `asset_impact: required`, the B-series writer must reserve stable,\nproduct-specific asset IDs (never generic names such as `image1`), provide an\n`asset_brief` and `visual_style_version`, and include an `## Asset assessment`\nsection explaining the assets' purpose, where they appear, the required visual\nstates/variants, source-of-truth ownership, and original-art acceptance checks.\nFor `not_applicable`, that section must explain why the scope needs no generated\nor source visual asset and explicitly prohibit incidental asset creation. This\nkeeps UI, illustration, icon, texture, sprite, audio-visual, and other product\nasset work visible in the implementation plan instead of discovering it midway\nthrough coding.\n\nEvery generated R-series runbook must also declare an audio assessment, even\nwhen audio is not needed:\n\n```yaml\naudio_impact: required # or not_applicable\naudio_ids: ember_menu_loop # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_brief: 30-second seamless instrumental menu cue # blank only when not_applicable\naudio_duration_seconds: 30 # 0 only when not_applicable\naudio_loop: required # required, not_required, or not_applicable\naudio_style_version: project-audio-v1\n```\n\nFor `audio_impact: required`, the writer must reserve stable cue IDs, cite the\nrelevant `04-audio-direction.md` section, describe the in-product trigger and\nmix/accessibility expectations, and assign a sensible duration and loop policy.\nThe Supervisor's separate local audio lane then creates a manifest, invokes\nACE-Step, and performs technical/provenance QA before coding begins. For\n`not_applicable`, every audio field has the stated empty/default form so an\notherwise unrelated task cannot silently generate music or sound effects.\n\nEach B-series authoring task may create at most seven R-series implementation\nrunbooks. It must stop after its assigned seven (or fewer), update the manifest,\nand leave remaining work for the next bounded batch.\n\nAn unresolved framework, legal, service, design, or other human gate is never\npermission for a B-series writer to omit its assigned R files or wait for an\nearlier B batch to be accepted. The writer produces the bounded contract now,\nrecords the gate and any R-to-R implementation dependency explicitly, and lets\nthe later R-series product-work run pause at that genuine decision. In short:\n**gates block implementation, not runbook authoring**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The initial collection contains only a bounded bootstrap wave; each\n  dispatcher expands at most one 250-contract domain shard, creates at most ten\n  new B-series authoring tasks plus one successor, then exits. It never attempts\n  to materialise the whole game plan.\n- There is exactly one valid B-series authoring runbook per allocated manifest\n  batch, and it creates no more than seven assigned R-series runbooks.\n- B-series runbooks never overwrite an existing R-series contract with a\n  conflicting ID; they stop and report mismatches.\n- Every generated B-series runbook includes its context packet, output list,\n  validation procedure, checkpoint/update procedure, and a clear stop condition.\n- Every generated B-series runbook states that it must author its allocated R\n  files despite unresolved implementation gates or unimplemented R\n  dependencies, retaining those gates in the R contract rather than stopping.\n- Both child-collection registration files exist, contain valid JSON with a\n  relative `runbooks_dir`, and point to the generated authoring and\n  implementation collections respectively.\n- R-series contracts use stable IDs and parse with the Supervisor runbook\n  loader; their declared dependencies match the manifest, every contract has\n  explicit `asset_impact` and `asset_ids` metadata, and asset-required\n  contracts have non-empty stable IDs. Every R contract also has non-empty,\n  valid `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, `authoring_batch`,\n  and `factory_stages` provenance metadata.\n- Every R-series contract has explicit valid audio metadata. Audio-required\n  contracts have stable IDs, a non-empty cue brief, duration, loop policy,\n  audio-style version, and a source link to the canonical audio direction.\n- The collection contains a final audit B-series task after all authoring\n  batches and catalogue expansions are complete, rather than pretending that\n  thousands of contracts can be reviewed in one generation step.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '60,165p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md && sed -n '115,205p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md && sed -n '92,175p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md && sed -n '1,180p' projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n### Versioned content and save schemas\n\nAll high-volume authored data uses a versioned, machine-validated package:\n\n```text\nContentPackage { packageId, semanticVersion, schemaVersion, localeDefault,\n  scenes[], exits[], dialogues[], quests[], encounters[], enemyDefinitions[],\n  itemDefinitions[], rewards[], localisation[], assetManifest[] }\nSaveSnapshot { schemaVersion, contentPackageId, contentVersion, slotId,\n  revision, checkpointId, campaign, quests, party, inventory, rewardLedger,\n  settingsReference?, checksum, committedAt }\n```\n\n- **Ownership and authoring:** designated game/content owners maintain source\n  data in repository-controlled files and original asset references. The exact\n  editor/format is an implementation choice; generated bundles are derived,\n  never hand-edited.\n- **Validation:** CI validates JSON/schema shape, unique stable IDs, required\n  fields, asset and localisation-key existence, valid quest predicates,\n  scene/spawn/exit targets, legal reward/item/enemy references, no duplicate\n  reward IDs, and reachability from opening scene to ending. It also rejects\n  missing required translations in any release locale and unsafe quest-item\n  removal paths.\n- **Relationship rules:** every required quest path has a reachable transition;\n  each locked exit predicate refers to an existing quest state; each encounter\n  has legal targets/actions and a completion path; all rewards resolve to\n  extant definitions. Tests include valid minimal package, each broken\n  reference class, and a graph traversal proving the authored campaign is\n  completable.\n- **Import/export:** P0 imports content only at build time through the\n  validator and packages it into the release. Player save export/import is not\n  promised; if added, it must use a versioned envelope, parse/validate before\n  write, never replace a valid save until confirmation, and reject untrusted\n  payloads safely.\n- **Compatibility:** each release declares supported content and save schema\n  ranges. Incompatible saves are quarantined with their original bytes and a\n  clear fallback/new-game action; a migration must create a new candidate and\n  validate it before promotion.\n\n## Commands, validation, idempotency, and concurrency\n\nThe core exposes typed intent commands such as `StartCampaign`,\n`ChooseAction`, `UseItem`, `Talk`, `AcceptQuest`, `ClaimReward`,\n`EnterExit`, `CommitCheckpoint`, `LoadSlot`, and `ApplySettings`. A command\ncontains an expected campaign revision and an interaction/action ID. The core\nreturns either a typed rejection without mutation or an ordered state/event\nresult with a new revision.\n\n- Validate session state, command shape, actor/target existence, availability,\n  eligibility, quest predicate, and expected revision before mutation. UI\n  selections are untrusted/stale inputs even though all execution is local.\n- Use stable `rewardId`/`grantId` ledger entries and interaction IDs. Retrying\n  an acknowledged reward, quest completion, or checkpoint returns the prior\n  result rather than granting twice.\n- One command is processed at a time per active campaign. Disable/debounce\n  duplicate controls while pending; compare expected revision on completion.\n  Visibility changes, gamepad repeats, and multiple tabs cannot interleave\n  transitions. A second tab must be warned/read-only or acquire an explicit\n  local slot lease; stale writers fail without replacing the latest revision.\n- Combat resolution uses an explicit deterministic seed/state recorded at\n  safe boundaries. It never persists an unresolved turn; a crash restores the\n  prior checkpoint, avoiding half-consumed items, half-applied damage, or\n  duplicate rewards.\n\n## Persistence, migration, and failure semantics\n\nSave commit is a write-ahead replacement protocol: serialize a complete\nsnapshot \u2192 validate checksum/schema/invariants \u2192 write candidate under a new\nrevision \u2192 verify read-back \u2192 mark current \u2192 retain prior known-good snapshot.\nImplementations must use browser storage semantics that make the final pointer\nswitch atomic, or emulate it with immutable revision records and a validated\ncurrent pointer. Never clear the prior save before the new pointer is valid.\n\n| Condition | Required behaviour |\n| --- | --- |\n| Storage quota, permission, or unavailable local storage | Keep session playable; show non-blocking save failure and retry guidance; do not claim persistence succeeded. |\n| Interrupted/crashed write | Ignore incomplete candidate, retain/reload prior confirmed snapshot, and show recovery state at next launch. |\n| Malformed/checksum-invalid save | Quarantine bytes and metadata; do not overwrite; offer last valid checkpoint/new game and support/export guidance where feasible. |\n| Migration failure or unsupported version | Preserve original, fail closed into quarantine, and offer clear version/fallback choices. |\n| Bad content package/reference | Fail build/CI; if discovered at runtime, stop the affected route, retain save, and offer title/retry rather than corrupting campaign state. |\n| Cache/network refresh failure | Continue with known-good cached release; explain first-install offline limitation without pretending an uncached release is playable. |\n| Application fault/crash loop | Error boundary offers retry, title, and safe recovery; diagnostics remain local unless explicitly consented and a future transport is approved. |\n\nMigration functions are ordered, pure transformations from one explicit schema\nversion to the next, with fixtures for every supported predecessor. They must\nbe idempotent or record the source version so a retry cannot apply a migration\ntwice. A release may remove old migrations only after a separately approved\nsupport/retention decision.\n\n## Trust, privacy, and security\n\n- Treat content, imported saves, URL parameters, browser events, service-worker\n  messages, and persisted bytes as untrusted. Validate and bound sizes before\n  parsing; never execute content as code or render dialogue via unsafe HTML.\n- Serve production assets over HTTPS with a restrictive content security policy,\n  no third-party scripts by default, dependency lock/review, and build-time\n  asset integrity/hash manifest. Do not embed credentials in the client.\n- Use same-origin storage isolation; minimise persisted data to game state and\n  chosen preferences. Do not collect names, contact data, precise location,\n  advertising IDs, account identifiers, payment data, or gameplay analytics in\n  P0.\n- Diagnostics default off where consent is required and must state fields,\n  purpose, retention, deletion, and transport before collection. A local\n  diagnostic record excludes free-text dialogue and complete save contents.\n- There is no authorization role in P0 because there is no server resource or\n  identity boundary. Locally, a player controls their browser profile; this is\nlevels.\n\n### 3. Narrative, quests, onboarding, and ending\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Dialogue` is `available \u2192 shown \u2192 acknowledged`;\n`Quest` is `unavailable \u2192 available \u2192 accepted \u2192 objective-complete \u2192\nclaimed \u2192 completed` (or `failed` only where authored); `TutorialStep` is\n`pending \u2192 presented \u2192 understood`; `Campaign` is `not-started \u2192 active \u2192\ncompleted`. Inputs are original characters, text, localisation keys, objective\npredicates, rewards, and ending sequence. Rules: tutorial teaches a battle and\nsaving before unrestricted progression; required quests cannot be abandoned;\ncompletion is idempotent. Dependencies are scenes, combat, inventory, UI, and\nsaves. Outcomes are clear objectives and a short finish. Edge cases: repeated\nNPC talk, dialogue after completion, missing translation, and an invalid quest\npredicate. **Boundary:** one authored story path; no branching campaign,\nseasonal narrative, or user-authored stories.\n\n### 4. Party combat, encounters, rewards, and balance\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Encounter` is `pending \u2192 active \u2192 player-turn \u2192\nresolution \u2192 won | lost | escaped-if-authored`; `Combatant` is `ready \u2192 acting\n\u2192 resolved \u2192 defeated`; `Reward` is `pending \u2192 granted`. Inputs are party and\nenemy definitions, actions, targeting, encounter placement, reward tables, and\nbalance values. Rules: only legal actions/targets resolve; turn order is visible;\nreward grants once; defeat returns to a safe checkpoint. Dependencies are party,\ninventory, quest transitions, audiovisual feedback, and saves. Outcome is a\nlearnable turn-based first battle and reliable progress. Edge cases: no legal\ntarget, empty item list, invalid action request, pause/focus loss, crash during\nresolution, and stale UI selection. **Boundary:** authored encounters only; no\nmultiplayer, ranked modes, live balance changes, or mid-combat save guarantee.\n\n### 5. Inventory, party progression, and economy\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `InventoryEntry` is `absent \u2192 acquired \u2192 usable |\nequipped \u2192 consumed-if-applicable`; `PartyMember` progresses through authored\nstates; `RewardGrant` is `unclaimed \u2192 applied`. Inputs are item definitions,\ndescriptions, icons, use/equip restrictions, and rewards. Rules: use validates\ntarget and eligibility before mutation; required quest items remain protected;\nduplicate grants are ignored by stable reward ID. Dependencies are combat,\nquests, UI, content validation, and saves. Outcome is meaningful reward use\nwithout dead ends. Edge cases: empty inventory, ineligible target, capacity\nlimit if selected, duplicate reward, and missing item definition. **Boundary:**\nsmall authored set; no crafting, trading, loot boxes, purchases, or destructive\ndiscard flow without approval.\n\n### 6. Save, recovery, and offline persistence\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `SaveSlot` is `empty \u2192 writing \u2192 valid \u2192 loading` or\n`quarantined`; `Checkpoint` is `eligible \u2192 committed`; recovery is `detect \u2192\npreserve \u2192 offer-fallback \u2192 restored | new-game`. Inputs are schema version,\ncampaign/quest/party/inventory/settings state, checkpoint triggers, and\nmigration rules. Rules: validate before replace; retain last known-good data;\nnever overwrite corruption; loading restores only safe scene boundaries; delete\nrequires explicit confirmation. Dependencies are every durable domain, PWA\nstorage, error UX, and release versioning. Outcome is confidence to stop and\nresume. Edge cases: quota/permission denial, malformed data, interrupted write,\nold schema, unavailable local storage, offline launch, and later remote conflict.\n**Boundary:** local durable saves and recovery; remote accounts, sync, cross-\ndevice merge, and cloud deletion policy await approval.\n\n### 7. Accessibility, localisation, and audiovisual feedback\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Preference` is `default \u2192 previewed \u2192 applied \u2192\npersisted`; `LocalePack` is `validated \u2192 packaged \u2192 active`; `FeedbackEvent`\nis emitted by action/scene/combat state. Inputs are accessible labels, text\nstyles, captions, visual settings, translations, original art/audio, and event\nbindings. Rules: settings are understandable and reversible; captions/text do\nnot convey essential information only through sound/colour; missing translation\nfalls back to the approved base language and is logged for content repair.\nDependencies are UI, content packaging, input, and storage. Outcome is readable,\ncontrollable play with clear feedback. Edge cases: unsupported preference,\nstorage failure, missing locale key, muted audio, contrast conflict, and narrow\nviewport. **Boundary:** the settings categories named in the brief and a\nlanguage-content pipeline; exact languages, remapping depth, ratings, and audio\nproduction scope remain decisions.\n\n### 8. PWA delivery, release safety, diagnostics, and quality operations\n\n**Entities/lifecycle:** `Release` is `built \u2192 validated \u2192 published \u2192 cached \u2192\nsuperseded`; `Cache` is `installing \u2192 ready \u2192 retained | replaced`; `Fault` is\n`caught \u2192 player-recovered \u2192 optionally-reported`. Inputs are asset manifests,\ncontent/save compatibility declarations, service-worker policy, error messages,\nminimal diagnostic schema, and test matrices. Rules: an update activates at a\ntitle/menu safe boundary after a confirmed save; failed refresh retains a\nknown-good cache; diagnostics minimise data and respect consent; supported\nbrowser/device/network and performance thresholds must be agreed before release\nacceptance. Dependencies are all packaged content, persistence, shell, privacy,\nand quality checks. Outcome is safe installation, offline continuation, update,\nand error recovery. Edge cases: declined install, first offline visit, stale\ncache, asset fetch failure, crash loop, diagnostics denial/deletion, and storage\npressure. **Boundary:** installable web/PWA and minimal crash recovery only; no\n- Settings save independently of campaign saves where storage permits. If persistence fails, keep the in-session choice, state that it will not persist, and preserve a usable default. Reset settings is confirmed and describes the affected preference categories.\n\n## Empty, error, recovery, destructive, and privacy-sensitive states\n\n| Situation | Experience requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| Empty inventory / no quest / no save | State what is empty, why it may be empty, and the next useful action: e.g., `No items yet\u2014explore the town and finish the first encounter.` No decorative blank panels. |\n| Invalid action, locked exit, unavailable target | Keep the player\u2019s state and turn intact; name the unmet requirement and return focus to the legal choices. Do not use a generic `Error` as the only explanation. |\n| Storage failure, corrupt save, or interrupted save | Never claim a save completed until confirmed. Retain the last valid checkpoint; show retry, return-to-title, and fallback/new-game paths. Quarantined saves are explained as preserved but unusable; recovery text avoids blame. |\n| Offline, install, cache, or update state | Explain whether the current cached version can play, whether an initial download is required, and that an update will wait for a save-safe title/menu boundary. Declining install or update does not block play on a valid cached/current release. |\n| Fault / crash recovery | Present plain-language retry, return to title, and safe-recovery actions. Preserve confirmed progress. A diagnostic option is optional and clearly separate from recovery. |\n| Delete a save | Require a confirmation dialog that names the slot, its progress/time where available, and that deletion is irreversible. Initial focus is `Cancel`; `Delete` is visually and semantically distinct and cannot be activated through a stale/repeated input. Only the selected local slot and associated recovery metadata are removed. |\n| New game over an active slot / reset settings | Explain precisely what will change. New game must use a separate slot or obtain explicit confirmation before replacing a selected slot. Settings reset affects preferences only, not campaign state. |\n| Diagnostics and local data | P0 sends no telemetry. Before any consent-gated local diagnostic record is created or exported, state purpose, included minimal fields, retention, deletion control, and that it does not affect play. `Clear diagnostic data` confirms the local-only effect. Never show save contents or dialogue in diagnostics UI. |\n\n## PWA-specific experience\n\nThe web and installed PWA share the campaign, controls, accessibility settings, semantic UI, and local-save behaviour. Installation is an optional convenience: the title/PWA status area explains availability and has a non-modal fallback when the browser offers no install prompt. Offline status is visible but not alarming. An uncached first visit tells the player that the game cannot begin offline until its assets finish downloading; a known-good installed/cache version continues if an update check fails.\n\nAn update notice appears only at a safe boundary (title or paused menu after a confirmed save) and says whether reloading is needed. It offers `Update now` and `Later`; it never reloads during combat, a save write, a modal choice, or essential dialogue. Cache refresh messaging does not imply that save data was refreshed, deleted, or synchronised.\n\n## Content and interaction review checklist\n\nBefore a content or UI change ships, review it against this contract: original provenance; clear next action and empty/error copy; keyboard, touch, mouse, gamepad, and semantic assistive-input operation; visible focus and accurate accessible names; contrast and non-colour cues; 44 CSS-px touch targets; 200% text/reflow; captions and reduced motion; safe save/update/recovery behaviour; destructive confirmation; and consent/minimisation for any privacy-sensitive interface.\n\n## Open decisions retained for approval\n\n- Exact content quantities, party size, localisation languages, full control-remapping depth, audio scope, and supported browser/device/assistive-technology matrix.\n- The legal, age/parental, regional, and certification policies that may change content warnings or accessibility obligations.\n- Account identity, remote sync, multiplayer, player safety/moderation, live operations, commerce, and analytics. These remain outside the offline P0 experience; no social, payment, reporting, account, or remote-data UI may be designed as committed functionality without approval.\n# Implementation catalogue index\n\nThis is the F012 implementation-authoring index for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**.\nThe machine-readable source is\n[`implementation-catalogue-index.json`](implementation-catalogue-index.json).\nIt decomposes only the first bounded shard; it does not author R-series\nrunbooks or approve any decision gate.\n\n## Scope and ownership rules\n\n- **SHARD-01 \u2014 Foundation and core contracts** contains 12 independently\n  verifiable contracts (limit: 250). It establishes framework-neutral seams,\n  deterministic data contracts, local persistence/recovery protocols, quality\n  controls, and documentation. It does not implement campaign behaviour,\n  player UI, PWA lifecycle, or release actions.\n- **Shared** owns campaign rules and platform-neutral contracts. **Web** owns\n  browser input, responsive layout, origin storage, and web builds. **PWA** is\n  a delivery/cache/install adaptation only: it reuses the shared game and web\n  UI, while owning its service-worker lifecycle. Save data and cache data are\n  deliberately separate.\n- `GATE-*` records block dependent authoring; they are not defaults. The\n  catalogue keeps connected capabilities out of P0 under `GATE-0006`.\n- Content must be original. The functional reference never authorises copied\n  names, text, lore, art, maps, layouts, music, or interaction choreography.\n\n## Current contracts\n\n| ID | Domain | Outcome | Prerequisites | Gate/status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| IMP-0001 | Foundation | Reproducible shared project baseline | \u2014 | GATE-0001 / gated |\n| IMP-0002 | Foundation | Core and adapter dependency seams | IMP-0001 | current |\n| IMP-0003 | Tests | Deterministic test/fixture harness | IMP-0001\u20130002 | current |\n| IMP-0004 | Data | Deterministic state/command/event contract | IMP-0002\u20130003 | current |\n| IMP-0005 | Content | Versioned content schema and validator | IMP-0001, 0003\u20130004 | current |\n| IMP-0006 | Persistence | Local save/recovery protocol | IMP-0002\u20130004 | GATE-0003 / gated |\n| IMP-0007 | Persistence | Pure migration runner | IMP-0005\u20130006 | GATE-0003 / gated |\n| IMP-0008 | Security | P0 connected-service exclusions | IMP-0002, 0004 | current |\n| IMP-0009 | Privacy | Local, redacted diagnostics boundary | IMP-0002\u20130003, 0006 | GATE-0005 / gated |\n| IMP-0010 | Accessibility | Semantic design-token contract | IMP-0001\u20130002 | GATE-0002/0004 / gated |\n| IMP-0011 | Content | Original-content provenance control | IMP-0005 | current + human review |\n| IMP-0012 | Documentation | Foundation boundary documentation | IMP-0002, 0004, 0006, 0008 | current |\n\nEach JSON contract has one title, domain, target allocation, requirement IDs,\nbounded outcome, prerequisite list, sole files/data/API ownership, forbidden\nscope, verification, human/external gate, complexity, and status. The only\ndependency direction is toward earlier contracts, so the current graph is\nacyclic.\n\n## Domain-expansion queue\n\n| Queue ID | Bounded domain (maximum contracts) | Dependency | Requirements/gate | Allocation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SHARD-02 | Campaign content and domain logic (250) | SHARD-01 | Core P0 campaign; GATE-0004 | Shared core/content; no UI |\n| SHARD-03 | Session, UI, input, and accessibility (250) | SHARD-01\u201302 | REQ-0005\u20130007, 0009\u20130010, 0012; GATE-0002\u20130004 | Shared UI model, Web adapters, inherited PWA UI |\n| SHARD-04 | PWA delivery, performance, operations, and release evidence (250) | SHARD-01\u201303 | REQ-0011\u20130012, NFR-0001/0003/0006/0009/0011/0012; GATE-0002/0005/0007 | Separate web build and PWA lifecycle |\n| SHARD-05 | Connected-scope decision package (250) | SHARD-01 | REQ-0014\u20130015; GATE-0006 | Hold; research/decision outputs only if authorised |\n\nThe JSON `requirement_coverage` map accounts for every canonical `REQ-*` and\n`NFR-*` as current, queued, gated, or held, naming the corresponding contract\nor expansion shard. No requirement is silently rejected or deferred.\n\n## Structural validation\n\nUse this check after edits:\n\n```sh\nnode -e 'const c=require(\"./projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\"); const ids=new Set(c.contracts.map(x=>x.id)); if (ids.size!==c.contracts.length || c.first_bounded_domain.contract_count>c.first_bounded_domain.contract_limit || c.expansion_queue.some(x=>x.max_contracts>250) || Object.keys(c.requirement_coverage).length!==27 || c.contracts.some(x=>x.prerequisites.some(p=>!ids.has(p)))) process.exit(1); console.log(\"catalogue structural check passed\")'\n```\n\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d78c852775c166f38fda7937116796d09e22fc26\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0005\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\n+dependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\n+authoring_batch: B0004\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No art or audio assets; reserve schema and provenance fields only for later original assets.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\n+validator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\n+can be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\n+it does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\n+expression.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\n+and R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\n+dependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\n+API, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\n+local-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or\n+cache implementation.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}/`.\n+- `tests/content/validation.*` and deterministic content graph fixtures.\n+- `docs/content-authoring.md`.\n+- The versioned content-package, asset/provenance-manifest, and validator API\n+  contracts.\n+\n+The content registry loads only a fully validated package and is read-only at\n+runtime. It does not own campaign state, save snapshots, preferences, browser\n+storage, PWA cache records, migrations, assets, or release packaging.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Model a package with stable package ID, semantic version, schema version,\n+default locale, scenes, exits, dialogues, quests, encounters, enemy and item\n+definitions, rewards, localisation, and an asset/provenance manifest. Validate\n+before registry publication: schema shape and bounded input, required fields,\n+unique stable IDs, locale-key and asset/provenance references, predicates,\n+scene/spawn/exit targets, reward/item/enemy references, duplicate reward IDs,\n+safe quest-item removal paths, and a reachable opening-to-ending path.\n+\n+Validation must return typed diagnostics and must not partially register an\n+invalid package. Build-time content import runs through this validator; derived\n+bundles are never hand edited. Runtime discovery of a bad package stops the\n+affected route, retains existing campaign/save data, and offers title or retry\n+rather than mutating or replacing state.\n+\n+Content compatibility is declared explicitly so the save/recovery owner can\n+compare a snapshot's content package/version without making the content\n+registry a persistence driver. Do not checkpoint, promote, overwrite,\n+quarantine, migrate, or delete a save here; those operations remain gated under\n+GATE-0003 and belong to R0006 and later R0007.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and PWA use the same shared validator, schema, and read-only registry. A\n+PWA cache is a delivery concern, not a content-validation result or save store;\n+neither target may bypass validation, write the active package at runtime, or\n+conflate cache failure with save recovery.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not create authored campaign content, dialogue, maps, art, audio, sprites,\n+icons, localisation copy, release bundles, gameplay algorithms, UI flows,\n+browser/PWA cache lifecycle, save drivers, migrations, export/import, cloud\n+sync, accounts, network clients, or storage policy. Do not resolve GATE-0003\n+or GATE-0004; content quantities, locales, and detail remain unapproved.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: this work defines schemas and validation\n+only. Do not create, reserve, source, or generate incidental visual, audio,\n+font, icon, illustration, texture, sprite, map, dialogue, or other product\n+asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank. The schema may reserve fields for\n+later original assets and provenance review without assigning an asset.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Load a valid minimal package and prove publication succeeds only after all\n+  validation phases complete.\n+- Use one deterministic invalid fixture for each reference class: duplicate ID,\n+  missing locale or asset/provenance record, invalid predicate, unresolved\n+  scene/exit/reward/item/enemy reference, unsafe quest-item removal, and\n+  unreachable ending; prove no invalid fixture is registered.\n+- Traverse a valid fixture from opening scene to ending and prove required\n+  transitions and rewards resolve.\n+- Verify a runtime-invalid-package result retains the existing state/save and\n+  provides title/retry recovery without selecting a storage API.\n+- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n+  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0005, dependencies\n+  match the manifest, owned paths are distinct from R0006, and every required\n+  section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain validator output for the valid package and every rejected reference\n+class, reachability traversal output, registry non-publication assertions,\n+runtime title/retry recovery evidence, and the pre-checkpoint loader,\n+provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- A valid minimal versioned package is the only kind of package the read-only\n+  registry can publish.\n+- Invalid IDs, references, predicates, localisation/provenance links, unsafe\n+  quest-item removal paths, and unreachable campaign graphs fail before play.\n+- Content/save compatibility is explicit while save, cache, migration, and\n+  storage decisions remain separate and GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 remains retained.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c8d2cd37f5e6077eddf6bb84b7eb1c50cd92b88d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0006\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Specify local save and recovery protocol\n+dependencies: R0002,R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0006\n+authoring_batch: B0004\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; this is a local data and recovery protocol.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the bounded, local save and recovery protocol for immutable revisions,\n+checksums, validated current pointers, known-good retention, quarantine,\n+separate preferences, explicit deletion, and save-safe boundaries. This is a\n+protocol and fixture contract, not approval to select a browser-storage API or\n+promise a quota, retention period, or migration-support window.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 provides the core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic clock and\n+persistence fixtures, and R0004 supplies the immutable versioned campaign\n+snapshot and command/revision contracts. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: storage\n+API, quota, support window, and recovery policy require human approval before\n+implementation selects or relies on them. The gate blocks implementation\n+choices, not this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/` protocol contracts.\n+- `src/platform/web/persistence/` adapter boundary.\n+- `tests/{core,platform}/save*` fault and recovery fixtures.\n+- `docs/save-and-recovery.md`.\n+- Snapshot/preference/quarantine schemas and snapshot-repository/recovery API.\n+\n+The shared layer owns snapshot shape, validation, compatibility, and recovery\n+semantics. The web adapter owns only the eventual approved local-storage\n+mechanism. PWA cache/install lifecycle, content registry, remote sync,\n+identity, diagnostics transport, and campaign transitions are not owned here.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a write-ahead replacement protocol: serialize a complete immutable\n+snapshot, validate checksum/schema/invariants, write a new revision candidate,\n+verify read-back, atomically mark a validated current pointer (or emulate it\n+with immutable records), and retain the prior known-good snapshot. Never clear\n+or overwrite the prior confirmed save until the new pointer is valid. Separate\n+preferences from campaign snapshots and never treat a cache record as a save.\n+\n+Validate bounded, untrusted persisted bytes before parsing or use. A malformed,\n+checksum-invalid, incompatible, or migration-failed candidate is preserved with\n+its metadata in quarantine; it never replaces a valid save. Recovery offers\n+the last valid checkpoint or a clear new-game/fallback route. Loading restores\n+only safe scene boundaries. A failed quota, permission, or unavailable-storage\n+attempt leaves the session playable, says persistence did not succeed, and\n+offers non-blocking retry guidance.\n+\n+Persist only at explicit safe boundaries: no unresolved combat turn or partial\n+command can become current. A stale writer must fail rather than replace the\n+latest revision. Deletion requires an explicit confirmation naming the selected\n+slot and its available progress/time; initial focus is Cancel, repeated/stale\n+input cannot activate Delete, and only that local slot and its recovery\n+metadata are removed.\n+\n+Migration transformations remain ordered pure candidate transformations and\n+are not implemented or approved here beyond their compatibility boundary; R0007\n+owns the migration runner. No cloud, account, sync, cross-device merge, cache\n+eviction, or export/import promise is introduced.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA share the same local snapshot, preference, validation,\n+quarantine, and recovery contract. The web adapter eventually binds an approved\n+same-origin storage mechanism; the PWA inherits it and must keep its\n+service-worker cache separate. A cache refresh or update failure neither\n+deletes, refreshes, nor synchronises save data, and no implementation may\n+claim persistence after an unconfirmed write.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not choose a storage API, quota, eviction guarantee, support window,\n+retention policy, or migration set before GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 approval. Do not\n+implement cloud sync, accounts, remote deletion, cross-device conflict\n+resolution, PWA cache lifecycle, release update flow, diagnostics transport,\n+content validation, gameplay, UI screens, product assets, or audio.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: local snapshots, protocol interfaces, and\n+fault fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental\n+visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other\n+product asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fault fixtures for interrupted write, failed read-back,\n+  checksum failure, malformed/oversized bytes, unsupported version, storage\n+  quota/permission/unavailable failures, stale writer, quarantine, retry, and\n+  selected-slot deletion confirmation.\n+- Prove each failure preserves the last valid snapshot, does not report a save\n+  as successful, keeps the session usable where possible, and exposes the\n+  required retry/title/fallback/new-game recovery choice.\n+- Prove a current-pointer promotion occurs only after candidate validation and\n+  read-back; prove preferences and PWA cache fixtures cannot be read as or\n+  overwrite a campaign snapshot.\n+- Prove a pending command or unresolved combat turn cannot be committed and a\n+  stale/repeated delete action cannot remove an unselected slot.\n+- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n+  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0006, dependencies\n+  match the manifest, owned paths do not overlap R0005's content boundary, and\n+  every required section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an\n+  R contract.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fault-fixture output, pre/post candidate and pointer\n+records, quarantine and recovery-path assertions, preference/save/cache\n+separation evidence, deletion-confirmation assertions, the retained\n+GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 record, and the pre-checkpoint loader, provenance,\n+dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Interrupted, invalid, incompatible, or failed save candidates cannot replace\n+  a validated current snapshot; the prior known-good snapshot is retained or\n+  malformed bytes are quarantined.\n+- Save snapshots, preferences, and PWA cache records remain separate, and\n+  local recovery presents clear retry, title, fallback, or new-game choices\n+  without claiming an unconfirmed save succeeded.\n+- Storage selection, quota, support window, migration policy, and recovery\n+  policy remain blocked by GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no remote, cache, or asset\n+  work is introduced.\n\nhook: PostToolUse\nhook: PostToolUse Failed\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d78c852775c166f38fda7937116796d09e22fc26\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0005\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\n+dependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\n+authoring_batch: B0004\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No art or audio assets; reserve schema and provenance fields only for later original assets.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\n+validator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\n+can be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\n+it does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\n+expression.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\n+and R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\n+dependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\n+API, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\n+local-save protoco