ct from R0006, and every required\n+  section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain validator output for the valid package and every rejected reference\n+class, reachability traversal output, registry non-publication assertions,\n+runtime title/retry recovery evidence, and the pre-checkpoint loader,\n+provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- A valid minimal versioned package is the only kind of package the read-only\n+  registry can publish.\n+- Invalid IDs, references, predicates, localisation/provenance links, unsafe\n+  quest-item removal paths, and unreachable campaign graphs fail before play.\n+- Content/save compatibility is explicit while save, cache, migration, and\n+  storage decisions remain separate and GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 remains retained.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..5259608314c9d1527122e135c08c20c502875e4a\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0006\n+sequence: 6\n+title: Specify local save and recovery protocol\n+dependencies: R0002,R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0006,REQ-0012,NFR-0002,NFR-0003,NFR-0005\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics,specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0006\n+authoring_batch: B0004\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No assets; this is a local data and recovery protocol.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Specify the bounded, local save and recovery protocol for immutable revisions,\n+checksums, validated current pointers, known-good retention, quarantine,\n+separate preferences, explicit deletion, and save-safe boundaries. This is a\n+protocol and fixture contract, not approval to select a browser-storage API or\n+promise a quota, retention period, or migration-support window.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0002 provides the core/adapter seam, R0003 provides deterministic clock and\n+persistence fixtures, and R0004 supplies the immutable versioned campaign\n+snapshot and command/revision contracts. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: storage\n+API, quota, support window, and recovery policy require human approval before\n+implementation selects or relies on them. The gate blocks implementation\n+choices, not this contract's authoring.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- `src/core/save/{schema,compatibility,migrations}/` protocol contracts.\n+- `src/platform/web/persistence/` adapter boundary.\n+- `tests/{core,platform}/save*` fault and recovery fixtures.\n+- `docs/save-and-recovery.md`.\n+- Snapshot/preference/quarantine schemas and snapshot-repository/recovery API.\n+\n+The shared layer owns snapshot shape, validation, compatibility, and recovery\n+semantics. The web adapter owns only the eventual approved local-storage\n+mechanism. PWA cache/install lifecycle, content registry, remote sync,\n+identity, diagnostics transport, and campaign transitions are not owned here.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Use a write-ahead replacement protocol: serialize a complete immutable\n+snapshot, validate checksum/schema/invariants, write a new revision candidate,\n+verify read-back, atomically mark a validated current pointer (or emulate it\n+with immutable records), and retain the prior known-good snapshot. Never clear\n+or overwrite the prior confirmed save until the new pointer is valid. Separate\n+preferences from campaign snapshots and never treat a cache record as a save.\n+\n+Validate bounded, untrusted persisted bytes before parsing or use. A malformed,\n+checksum-invalid, incompatible, or migration-failed candidate is preserved with\n+its metadata in quarantine; it never replaces a valid save. Recovery offers\n+the last valid checkpoint or a clear new-game/fallback route. Loading restores\n+only safe scene boundaries. A failed quota, permission, or unavailable-storage\n+attempt leaves the session playable, says persistence did not succeed, and\n+offers non-blocking retry guidance.\n+\n+Persist only at explicit safe boundaries: no unresolved combat turn or partial\n+command can become current. A stale writer must fail rather than replace the\n+latest revision. Deletion requires an explicit confirmation naming the selected\n+slot and its available progress/time; initial focus is Cancel, repeated/stale\n+input cannot activate Delete, and only that local slot and its recovery\n+metadata are removed.\n+\n+Migration transformations remain ordered pure candidate transformations and\n+are not implemented or approved here beyond their compatibility boundary; R0007\n+owns the migration runner. No cloud, account, sync, cross-device merge, cache\n+eviction, or export/import promise is introduced.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+Web and installed PWA share the same local snapshot, preference, validation,\n+quarantine, and recovery contract. The web adapter eventually binds an approved\n+same-origin storage mechanism; the PWA inherits it and must keep its\n+service-worker cache separate. A cache refresh or update failure neither\n+deletes, refreshes, nor synchronises save data, and no implementation may\n+claim persistence after an unconfirmed write.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not choose a storage API, quota, eviction guarantee, support window,\n+retention policy, or migration set before GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 approval. Do not\n+implement cloud sync, accounts, remote deletion, cross-device conflict\n+resolution, PWA cache lifecycle, release update flow, diagnostics transport,\n+content validation, gameplay, UI screens, product assets, or audio.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`: local snapshots, protocol interfaces, and\n+fault fixtures require no product asset. Do not create or reserve incidental\n+visual, source, audio, icon, illustration, font, texture, sprite, map, or other\n+product asset; `asset_ids` and audio IDs remain blank.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Run deterministic fault fixtures for interrupted write, failed read-back,\n+  checksum failure, malformed/oversized bytes, unsupported version, storage\n+  quota/permission/unavailable failures, stale writer, quarantine, retry, and\n+  selected-slot deletion confirmation.\n+- Prove each failure preserves the last valid snapshot, does not report a save\n+  as successful, keeps the session usable where possible, and exposes the\n+  required retry/title/fallback/new-game recovery choice.\n+- Prove a current-pointer promotion occurs only after candidate validation and\n+  read-back; prove preferences and PWA cache fixtures cannot be read as or\n+  overwrite a campaign snapshot.\n+- Prove a pending command or unresolved combat turn cannot be committed and a\n+  stale/repeated delete action cannot remove an unselected slot.\n+- Before recording the B0004 checkpoint, validate the runbook loader parses\n+  this front matter, provenance is non-empty and maps to IMP-0006, dependencies\n+  match the manifest, owned paths do not overlap R0005's content boundary, and\n+  every required section is present. Stop on any mismatch; never overwrite an R contract.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+Retain deterministic fault-fixture output, pre/post candidate and pointer\n+records, quarantine and recovery-path assertions, preference/save/cache\n+separation evidence, deletion-confirmation assertions, the retained\n+GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 record, and the pre-checkpoint loader, provenance,\n+dependency, ownership, and required-section validation record.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- Interrupted, invalid, incompatible, or failed save candidates cannot replace\n+  a validated current snapshot; the prior known-good snapshot is retained or\n+  malformed bytes are quarantined.\n+- Save snapshots, preferences, and PWA cache records remain separate, and\n+  local recovery presents clear retry, title, fallback, or new-game choices\n+  without claiming an unconfirmed save succeeded.\n+- Storage selection, quota, support window, migration policy, and recovery\n+  policy remain blocked by GATE-0003 / DEC-0003; no remote, cache, or asset\n+  work is introduced.\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"Created the allocated B0004 implementation contracts R0005 and R0006 only, with retained GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 storage boundaries and pre-checkpoint validation requirements.\",\"changed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\"],\"test_result\":\"Passed: Supervisor runbook loader, provenance/dependency/required-section assertions, manifest allocation and retained-gate/mismatch-guard assertions, whitespace checks, and assigned-path count check.\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"Inspected the canonical brief, specification, allocation manifest, catalogue, F014 requirements, and prior R-series contracts before authoring.\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"loader, provenance, dependency, and required-section checks passed\\nmanifest allocation, gate-retention, and mismatch-guard checks passed\\nwhitespace checks passed\\nonly assigned B0004 runbook paths exist\",\"browser_log\":\"Not applicable: this authoring task changes implementation-runbook contracts only.\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[{\"criterion\":\"R0005 and R0006 are the only generated contracts and match their two IMP allocations.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Created only projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md and R0006.md; focused check confirmed exactly those assigned paths and manifest mappings R0005\u2192IMP-0005 and R0006\u2192IMP-0006.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Both contracts retain the save/storage gate and make no incidental asset work.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Both runbooks explicitly retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003 and declare asset_impact/audio_impact as not_applicable with explicit incidental-asset prohibitions.\"},{\"criterion\":\"Loader, provenance, dependency, ownership, and required-section validation completes before checkpointing.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Both contracts require these checks before B0004 checkpointing; Supervisor loader and focused provenance/dependency/required-section assertions passed.\"},{\"criterion\":\"A mismatch stops rather than overwrites an R contract.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":\"Both contracts require stopping on a mismatch and never overwriting an R contract; focused mismatch-guard assertion passed.\"}],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/02-feature-model.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/04-experience-contract.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json\",\"runbooks/F014.md\"],\"updated_files\":[\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\"],\"summary\":\"The two requested runbooks are the user-facing implementation documentation. No README, plan, or manifest change was needed because the existing manifest already allocates these exact immutable paths and this task required creating only them.\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"Not applicable: no browser product behavior or browser test scope changed; these are domain-contract authoring artifacts.\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d78c852775c166f38fda7937116796d09e22fc26\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,129 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0005\n+sequence: 5\n+title: Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\n+dependencies: R0001,R0003,R0004\n+requirement_ids: REQ-0002,REQ-0008,NFR-0007,NFR-0008\n+source_specifications: specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas,specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\n+source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0005\n+authoring_batch: B0004\n+factory_stages: F011,F012,F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No art or audio assets; reserve schema and provenance fields only for later original assets.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Define the shared, versioned content-package schema, read-only registry, and\n+validator that reject malformed or internally inconsistent content before it\n+can be loaded for play. The contract validates structure and relationships;\n+it does not author a town, dungeon, dialogue, map, encounter, or other campaign\n+expression.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+R0001 provides the project boundary, R0003 provides deterministic fixtures,\n+and R0004 provides versioned campaign-state envelopes. They are implementation\n+dependencies, not authoring blockers. Retain GATE-0003 / DEC-0003: save storage\n+API, quota, support-window, and recovery policy decisions remain owned by the\n+local-save protocol. This content contract neither chooses nor writes a save or\n+cache implementation.\n+\n+## Ownership